    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="b30a85ca-8e63-5b60-8800-c7e13c34afee" activityNameId="df1aec29-3ea5-56ee-9d61-c994b64ae68d" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Sewer system, construction, cast iron pipe, DN 300, profile 1</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Sewer system, construction, cast iron pipe, DN 300, profile 1
Modern Swiss und European technologies are applied to building machines, material production and building processes. 
UUID: 546a8918-88e3-4c98-a480-cfc81812587a
This process models 1 meter of installed sewer infrastructure with cast iron pipe and a trench depth of 3 meters. This process includes the production phase (A1–A3) and the construction phase/ transport (A4–A5) for one linear meter of installed cast iron pipe, including trench excavation and backfilling. Disposal and deconstruction processes are excluded and modelled separately specific for each sewer system type. The operation of similar types of building machines across different processes is aggregated to one process.
Location: Switzerland
Technology: DN 300, profile 1 according to SIA 190.Trench depth 3 meters. Cast iron pipe, 300 mm, outer diameter 319 mm, wall thickness 9.6 mm, 67 kg/m, 7200 kg/m³
Time period: Review of data currency scheduled after 5 years.
Production volume: 
Sampling: 
Extrapolations: None
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_546a8918-88e3-4c98-a480-cfc81812587a.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
